select` (or `omarchy-shell shell summon omarchy.menu` with a select payload), then press Enter: the select caller receives the highlighted option, the confirmation is gone and no desktop file is removed"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The test and the harness run the real handler bodies under node vm with Qt.callLater run synchronously. In Qt, cancelDelete() (Menu.qml:865) and openDmenu() (Menu.qml:948) each queue keyCatcher.forceActiveFocus() for later, and the dialog's own focus handling lives in ConfirmDialog.qml. Both queue the same target, so the order should not matter, but no test in this package drives the summon through real IPC in a running shell and presses a key afterwards.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":865},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":948},{"id":"shell/Ui/ConfirmDialog.qml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-VJR1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: on a real Quickshell, does the next key after a summon over the confirmation reach the new prompt?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Live summon over a raised uninstall confirmation\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:open"],"scenario":"with the confirmation raised on the root menu, summon the root route again (keybind pressed twice): the confirmation closes and nothing is removed; pressing Delete again raises it again"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"A second press of the menu keybind sends a route summon for the current menu. With the PR it cancels the pending confirmation like any other summon, so the user must press Delete again to uninstall. VJR1 states this for every summon; whether a maintainer wants that for a same-route summon is a product question, not a test result.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":34},{"id":"SW-REQ-261002-VJR1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: is dismissing the confirmation also right when the summon re-opens the menu the user is already in?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Same-route summon over the confirmation\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent (disclosure effects_unavailable), so call-path statements here come from reading the code. The test and the harness replay the real Menu.qml and ConfirmDialog.qml functions under node vm.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":22}],"severity":"info","title":"Analysis bounds: no change-effects analysis for QML","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"Evaluated 15d3c8b2 = proof baseline 49cd12b0 + b8938c42 (upstream 09bfcda4: the 3-line hunk in Menu.qml and the new test; its diff is line-for-line identical to the upstream PR diff, re-checked against `gh pr diff`) + proof work (VJR1 and its variables, spec conformance review REVIEW-261002-MV7M, evidence-backed trace re-reviews of the Menu.qml requirements, KI-MENU-OPEN-LEAVES-CONFIRM marked fixed with the PR's test as its in-suite reproducer, the static-check removal, the harness key events and 6 inputs, 9 annotation lines in the test that exist only on the mirror, known-issue evidence re-stamped and history entries put in time order after the replay) + an empty record commit. This round the mirror was rebuilt on 49cd12b0, which merges upstream `quattro` at 393a43d4 (#6951: bin/omarchy-upgrade-to-quattro and its test