e, line 115) and cite anchor CNF1 (current_deployment_relevance, line 118), but on this mirror CNF1 is removed from that script and the script is no longer an evidence manifest, so both sentences describe the baseline only; the same note (line 118) names upstream a85e29ab as this baseline's product code, while 49cd12b0 carries upstream `quattro` at 393a43d4 (that refresh does not touch Menu.qml, so the open() behaviour it describes is unchanged; the baseline record has the same lag). (2) risk is data_integrity (the mirror's own grading, justified in its 2 Oct history entry), while the later severity justification carried from the baseline (3 Oct, line 81) says the grade comes from correctness, the baseline's risk value. Both reach medium, so the severity is unaffected. Also, remediation and notes name the mirror by an internal label rather than PR #14054. Not edited by this review.","refs":[{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-OPEN-LEAVES-CONFIRM.yaml","kind":"file","line":115},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-OPEN-LEAVES-CONFIRM.yaml","kind":"file","line":118},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-OPEN-LEAVES-CONFIRM.yaml","kind":"file","line":14},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-OPEN-LEAVES-CONFIRM.yaml","kind":"file","line":81},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-uninstall-confirm-test.sh","kind":"file","line":93}],"severity":"low","title":"Opinion: KI-MENU-OPEN-LEAVES-CONFIRM on this mirror is consistent in its status, severity and evidence; two pieces of carried-over wording are stale","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:72ac7d49b1ffe0c7f677f69be66c2e72aa4939853fc195c9af42807c54e2461d","packageIdentity":"epkg-33cdff8c25cb050c7b00ff5a7f2429b58b6044fee8c2309f97bc405aa53a8ca6","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"A one-line guard reusing the dialog's own Cancel path, pinned by a test that fails on the baseline, 57/57 tests passing and a behaviour comparison whose 3 differences are all classified intended. Medium, not low, because 4 prevents_ready disclosures remain (the unapproved compat findings), Menu.qml has no engine-measured code MC/DC, and the fix is not driven through a live shell in this package. Not merge approval."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":11,"rationale":"Drives the fix through real IPC and Qt's deferred focus in a running shell.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":29},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-acceptance-test.sh","kind":"file"}],"title":"Live summon over a raised uninstall confirmation"},{"forClaim":12,"rationale":"Pins the chosen behaviour for a repeated keybind so a maintainer can confirm or change it.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":34}],"title":"Same-route summon over the confirmation"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** omacom/omarchy#14054 (head 09bfcda4) fixes #14052: an uninstall confirmation left up stayed over the next menu summon, and the Enter meant for the new prompt uninstalled the app. open() now runs cancelDelete() when the confirmation is up, before it opens the prompt or route (Menu.qml:29). The rest of the mirror is proof work (SW-REQ-261002-VJR1, reviews, the fixed known issue, harness inputs) on baseline 49cd12b0, which carries upstream `quattro` at 393a43d4.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Audit verdict at the head: pass (run run-d2533687). Test results current: 57 tests, 57 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; all 32 changed requirements are observed_pass; 31 obligation cells observed_pass, 17 not_linked (no tagged test). The PR's test passes at the head (10 ok) and fails on the 49cd12b0 Menu.qml (re-run by the reviewer). The 7 behaviour-comparison tests (harness + 6 inputs) passed; a re-run of the 6 inputs reproduces the 3 differences. Code-level MC/DC does not cover Menu.qml, so diffCoverage measures 0 changed decisions.\n\n**Compatibility.** All four compat sources ran. 4 unapproved findings (prevents_ready): 3 differential (cf-58419914dab2f835, cf-64edcd0cc0114af1, cf-c57a38ab9ab3f83e), classified intended against VJR1: an input, route or select summon over the confirmation; base uninstalls on Enter, head removes nothing. 1 removed_behavior (cf-4d41f5e4cae16ee6): a static check in the out-of-scope proof-of-concept script that pinned the bug. test_diff and mcdc_diff report none. Auditor notes call all 4 acceptable (each recorded 5 times); those are notes, not approvals.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Approve or reject each compat finding. Does the next key reach the new prompt in a live shell (not run here)? Is dismissing the confirmation wanted for a same-route summon?\n\n**Traceability.** Every in-scope changed file maps to a requirement (9/9); coherence single; no spec-gap candidates. 30 of 32 requirements are file-level code_changed matches. The fixed known issue is consistent in status, severity and evidence; two poc_quality notes (CNF1; a85e29ab where the baseline is 393a43d4) and one severity justification are stale.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** coverage_unmeasured (the .events inputs are data), changed_files_out_of_scope, checks_skipped (13 by configuration) and effects_unavailable (QML) inform only.\n\n**Readiness** is not_assessed; next decision human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), reviewer authority. Nothing here is an approval."}
